  "description": "The ground-truth method for checking what reeval records about a harness against what actually happened: run a real attempt, collect the gateway traffic, the CLI's on-disk state and its native stream, diff all three against the run record and transcript signal by signal, and file a gap for each mismatch. Use when adding or bumping a harness, filling its telemetry declarations, or when a token, cost or transcript number looks wrong.",
